Take the NEON paths when building with MSVC for ARM64.

MSVC on ARM64 defines _M_ARM64 but neither __ARM_NEON nor __aarch64__, so
simd_headers.hpp included no SIMD header and simd.hpp stopped at
#error "Implement me." on Windows arm64. MSVC ships arm64_neon.h with the
standard intrinsic names (vld1q_f32, vpaddq_f32, ...), so include it and
define the two macros the vendored math code tests for. clang-cl defines
both itself and keeps using arm_neon.h. Needed for the PyroWave decoder in
the Windows arm64 build; no change for x86 or Linux.

diff --git a/Granite/math/simd_headers.hpp b/Granite/math/simd_headers.hpp
index 07dcefc3..04fbd8f3 100644
--- a/Granite/math/simd_headers.hpp
+++ b/Granite/math/simd_headers.hpp
@@ -45,4 +45,16 @@
 #include <xmmintrin.h>
 #elif defined(__ARM_NEON)
 #include <arm_neon.h>
+#elif defined(_MSC_VER) && defined(_M_ARM64)
+// MSVC targeting ARM64 defines _M_ARM64 but neither __ARM_NEON nor __aarch64__,
+// which the NEON paths in simd.hpp and muglm.cpp test for. Its arm64_neon.h
+// provides the standard intrinsic names, so take the NEON paths there too.
+// (clang-cl defines both macros itself and is handled above.)
+#include <arm64_neon.h>
+#ifndef __ARM_NEON
+#define __ARM_NEON 1
+#endif
+#ifndef __aarch64__
+#define __aarch64__ 1
+#endif
 #endif
